WEBVTT

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:13.090
Bring them over here.

00:00:13.180 --> 00:00:14.260
-Got it.
-That way?

00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:19.770
We shall have a banquet to celebrate
the victory of our army!

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:21.640
Bring out the food and drinks!

00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:23.850
-Put that over there.
-Thanks for your help.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.230
Keep a watch on it.

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.070
What are you doing over there?

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.030
I wasn't feeling well, so I was resting.

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:40.870
I'm okay now.

00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:42.910
We're short-staffed.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:44.210
You should help.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.460
Yes.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:57.510
Escape from here?

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.010
What do you mean?

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:03.180
Prince Rudo will never forgive you.

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:05.480
It's dangerous for you to stay.

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:08.020
But...

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.030
The way he looked
when he was watching you two...

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.240
<i>I've never seen anyone look so scary!</i>

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:23.290
Tonight, after the banquet is over,

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.160
you two should run away.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.830
Luckily, this area has dense fog
in the morning.

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:31.630
-It's your chance to escape.
-What about you?

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.550
What are you going to do?

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.680
I...

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:39.430
gave my life to you, Miss Finis.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:43.140
Your happiness is my only wish.

00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:46.230
That's what keeps me going in life.

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:47.690
I...

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.940
I need you with me!

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:51.570
I know.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:54.610
I'll catch up with you later.

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:00.070
Corte...

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:48.220
THE SONG OF MORTALITY

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.310
<i>Ash City...</i>

00:03:50.770 --> 00:03:51.980
<i>Since ancient times,</i>

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:56.690
this city has been covered with ash.
It never clears.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:03:59.780
It's cursed, right?

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:03.110
Searching for Finis is going
to be hard work.

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:06.990
Look.

00:04:07.530 --> 00:04:10.660
It's an ancient mural of a war.

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:14.620
No matter the era,
there are always wars raging.

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:16.920
Is that...

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:18.920
A girl?

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:22.840
You're right. And she's not wearing armor.

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:31.640
<i>She creates the world</i>

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:36.060
<i>She destroys the world</i>

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:40.440
<i>When she sings, the world is reborn</i>

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:45.570
<i>When she sings, the world is destroyed</i>

00:04:45.660 --> 00:04:49.660
<i>The goddess</i>

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:52.290
<i>Of ancient times</i>

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:58.420
This is a legendary song
that all Court Minstrels know.

00:04:59.090 --> 00:05:00.710
It's from a long time ago.

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.420
A goddess who destroys the world?

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:06.930
What a sad song.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:10.060
It's just a legend.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:14.890
The real reason the world was destroyed
was because of a meteor.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:16.310
A meteor?

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:17.810
It's a star.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.860
-A star fell from the sky.
-Huh? Are you talking about that?

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.990
That fell from the sky?!

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:27.280
No way something like that could fall
from the sky.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.910
Good.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:30.990
What's wrong, Monica?

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.290
Well, that star has always been there.

00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:38.250
Was it always that big?

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.300
-It's always been like that, right?
-It's expanding.

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:48.680
Hey, hey.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:52.510
It's scientifically impossible
for a star to expand!

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:54.680
I'm copying Al.

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.100
He would say that.

00:06:04.480 --> 00:06:05.740
Let's look for Finis.

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.250
-Hey, bring some over here, too.
-Leader!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:20.250
Drink up!

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:23.420
Stop calling me "Leader."

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:27.220
What are you talking about?!
You're our leader, right?

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:28.550
Right, everyone?!

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:30.180
Yeah!

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:40.350
Hey, Leader, once the war ends,
why don't you team up with us?

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:44.980
Working as a knight in the Capital
is stifling, isn't it?

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:46.860
You're strong.

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:50.490
If you teamed up with us,
no one could stop us.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:56.410
Thanks for the offer,
but I have a different road to follow.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:07:00.290
Why? Your life would be full
of excitement every day.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.170
Well, if you ever need us,

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.840
call us anytime.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:06.550
Let's fight together again.

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.720
Sure. Thanks.

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:14.010
By the way,

00:07:14.430 --> 00:07:16.600
I haven't seen Prince Rudo around.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:18.930
If he were here, this wouldn't be fun.

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:21.190
Hey, you guys!

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:23.440
Let's drink the night away!

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:24.520
Yeah!

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:34.530
You're late!

00:07:35.490 --> 00:07:38.410
-I apologize.
-Hurry up and give it to the prince.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:40.710
Tell him it's from me.

00:07:41.580 --> 00:07:42.960
-Yes.
-Wait!

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:45.340
Corte.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:49.630
If you're going to bring him something,
it should be this,

00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:51.590
wine of the finest quality.

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.260
Excuse me.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:00.930
I've brought wine.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:03.770
Please allow me to pour you some.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:22.500
This wine is of the finest quality
and suited for a ruler

00:08:22.580 --> 00:08:24.120
of the continent like you.

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:28.460
Please enjoy a taste of the prosperity
of the Capital.

00:08:41.060 --> 00:08:43.480
When this banquet ends
and tomorrow comes,

00:08:43.940 --> 00:08:45.770
everything will be different.

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:47.730
Yes.

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:51.070
I'm going with you.
Leaving everything behind.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:56.820
I'll have a horse waiting in the forest.

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.660
-Go there in the morning.
-Okay.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:02.500
There are many places I want to take you.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:04.660
The world is big.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.500
And there's someone I want you to meet.

00:09:07.880 --> 00:09:10.590
I want to leave the continent.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.550
I bet there are lots of flowers
I've never seen before.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:16.680
But I bet you'd get lost again.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:18.470
You're so mean.

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:20.180
I'll be fine.

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:23.390
See? Corte will come, too.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:26.190
Corte has a hard job.

00:09:29.230 --> 00:09:30.860
<i>Is it really that odd?</i>

00:09:32.940 --> 00:09:35.320
To see me drink wine?

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:39.120
No. Although this wine is
of the finest quality,

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:42.790
-I was worried whether you'd like it.
-You're Finis's attendant, right?

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:44.000
Yes.

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:47.960
I heard that when she uses
the power of songs, her life shortens.

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:52.710
She probably... only has enough strength
to sing one more song.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:56.340
-So...
-Why did you bring me wine?

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:59.300
It's from the military advisor.

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:02.970
He said he wanted to celebrate
your victory.

00:10:03.560 --> 00:10:07.140
Do you know what members
of the royal family learn first?

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:08.560
Excuse me?

00:10:09.310 --> 00:10:10.190
Etiquette?

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:12.020
The military arts?

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:14.570
These are all necessary.

00:10:15.740 --> 00:10:19.280
However, the most important thing
is something else.

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.200
It's knowledge about poison.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:27.500
The royal family is always a target
for other countries.

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:31.380
That's why we're taught about all kinds
of assassination methods.

00:10:31.960 --> 00:10:35.840
One method that is
particularly effective... is poison.

00:10:37.340 --> 00:10:39.340
Whether you hire more guards

00:10:39.430 --> 00:10:42.050
or protect yourself
with an army of millions,

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:46.310
someone could always kill you easily
with poison.

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.520
Bread, soup...

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.560
and...

00:10:52.730 --> 00:10:53.980
wine.

00:11:11.210 --> 00:11:13.880
What? It really is poison!

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:18.210
Don't worry.

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:22.800
I'll make sure I tell Finis and Leobolt.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:42.450
Miss Finis...

00:11:56.540 --> 00:11:59.170
I wonder where Finis is.

00:11:59.760 --> 00:12:02.470
I wonder if the Capital Army is giving her
a hard time.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:06.890
Allu, I'm sleepy.

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:09.060
Seriously?! Everyone, be careful.

00:12:10.350 --> 00:12:13.440
Whenever Monica senses danger,
she falls asleep.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:18.270
In other words, the fact that she's sleepy
means that danger is near.

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:20.940
No way she could sense
something like that--

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:23.240
It's true!

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:24.570
Who are you?

00:12:29.700 --> 00:12:30.660
Wow.

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:40.050
Hey. If the Capital Army is here,
that means Finis must be, too.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:41.840
Over there.

00:12:43.380 --> 00:12:44.430
A camp.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:49.640
-How should we look for her?
-The morning fog is dense.

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:54.890
At dawn, the fog and dust together
should provide us some cover.

00:12:55.230 --> 00:12:57.900
Okay. Let's go back to the carriage
and rest.

00:12:58.520 --> 00:12:59.360
Okay.

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:07.570
<i>Have you seen Corte?</i>

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:12.000
No. I haven't seen her since she took
some wine to Prince Rudo.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.750
To Prince Rudo?

00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.750
There aren't enough attendants
to go around,

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:19.630
so she might have been called
into another tent.

00:13:19.710 --> 00:13:20.550
I see.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:29.850
Hey. Get in.

00:13:33.220 --> 00:13:36.850
Why do prisoners get to stay in tents
while we sleep outside?

00:13:37.560 --> 00:13:40.230
Even though they're enemies,
we should treat them well.

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:41.480
Come on.

00:13:41.730 --> 00:13:43.740
You're too naive, Leader.

00:13:47.280 --> 00:13:48.660
Stay where you are.

00:13:49.320 --> 00:13:52.490
You have all earned honor in this war.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:55.330
Especially you, Henry Leobolt.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:57.710
You're a true hero.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:04.840
By the way,
are the prisoners over here?

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:06.840
Yes. In that tent there.

00:14:07.510 --> 00:14:09.220
Let me have a look.

00:14:09.760 --> 00:14:11.510
Leobolt, follow me.

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:18.390
That's weird.

00:14:18.900 --> 00:14:22.320
Why would the prince check
on prisoners in the middle of the night?

00:14:22.690 --> 00:14:24.820
Who knows? I'm gonna take a piss.

00:14:38.710 --> 00:14:40.960
It's so hard to see now.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:42.340
Let's go.

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:13.160
Where are you going?

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:17.290
Why are you dressed like that?

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:19.410
Uh, well...

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:22.500
I just woke up and wanted to wash my face.

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.090
I see.

00:15:25.550 --> 00:15:28.460
Good timing. I wanted to ask you
to do something.

00:15:29.380 --> 00:15:30.300
Follow me.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:37.390
What a morning, huh?

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:39.890
Finis is here, right?

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:43.770
I haven't seen her yet.

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:45.150
Me neither.

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:47.070
Does she even exist?

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:49.650
I heard she's a songstress
with miraculous power.

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:52.280
-Did you hear that?
-Yeah.

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:54.370
So, Finis really is here.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:15:56.410
Let's look for her.

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:58.410
That's so pretty.

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:00.540
You're right.

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:03.540
It's different from the others.

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.510
She's not here.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:17.100
Where are you, Finis?

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:28.650
Last night, enemy prisoners tried
to escape.

00:16:29.150 --> 00:16:31.070
We were able to kill them,

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:33.400
but we suffered a few casualties, too.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:40.660
What the enemy soldiers did
is unforgivable.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:43.540
But I don't want to hold any grudges.

00:16:44.540 --> 00:16:47.750
So... we'll have you use
the Song of Flame...

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:52.340
to cremate these enemy soldiers.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:53.800
Me?

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:58.760
Then I'll put an end to it...

00:16:59.560 --> 00:17:00.770
to this war...

00:17:01.810 --> 00:17:03.180
and the power of songs.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:07.940
You only have enough power
to sing one more song, right?

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:13.030
I'm sorry for everything, Finis.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:16.360
You're free now.

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:19.490
You can live however you like.

00:17:20.280 --> 00:17:21.120
So...

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:27.250
Please, sing one last song.

00:17:29.840 --> 00:17:30.920
I'll do it.

00:17:40.220 --> 00:17:45.690
<i>As the flame burns</i>
<i>A fleeting heartbeat</i>

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:52.440
<i>As the flame burns</i>
<i>Memories melt together</i>

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:56.450
<i>Be a flame</i>

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:00.240
<i>That swallows everything</i>

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:04.910
<i>My dear flame</i>

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.630
There's no way... he's still alive.

00:18:35.190 --> 00:18:36.780
No!

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:40.240
Oh, dear!

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:43.200
Isn't that Henry from the Leobolt family?

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:45.200
How strange.

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:46.120
Why...?

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:48.750
Why?!

00:18:52.000 --> 00:18:53.380
Finis...

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:56.630
The Song of Water! I'll put out the fire!

00:18:59.720 --> 00:19:02.680
No! If you sing, you'll die!

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:04.310
But, Henry!

00:19:07.430 --> 00:19:09.810
No. No!

00:19:12.230 --> 00:19:15.020
Finis... I can hear your voice...

00:19:18.690 --> 00:19:19.650
singing...

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:30.210
I must thank you, Finis.

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:33.460
We rid ourselves of the meddlers.

00:19:34.040 --> 00:19:39.220
Now that you've sung your last song,
you're just an empty shell.

00:19:40.590 --> 00:19:42.340
It's too bad.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:45.970
However, I have no need
for a woman who can't sing.

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:49.730
Go kill yourself or get lost,
whichever you prefer.

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:54.900
<i>The darkness</i>
<i>That beckons death</i>

00:19:56.150 --> 00:19:58.820
<i>Dwells within my body now</i>

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:04.240
<i>My blood cries in sorrow</i>

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:09.330
What? I thought you can't use
the power of songs anymore!

00:20:09.410 --> 00:20:10.960
<i>And awakens the Holy Flame</i>

00:20:17.840 --> 00:20:20.550
-What's going on?
-I have a bad feeling about this.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:22.340
Hey. Over there!

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:32.100
<i>Drown out the sound of a budding wish</i>

00:20:33.850 --> 00:20:38.980
<i>With your cries</i>

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:45.410
<i>There is no hope</i>

00:20:46.410 --> 00:20:48.830
-What's that?!
-The sky...

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:51.830
<i>Despair is our only savior</i>

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:57.040
It's falling from the sky!

00:20:57.130 --> 00:20:59.000
-Run away!
-Wait!

00:20:59.590 --> 00:21:02.550
Archers! Stop her! Kill her!

00:21:02.630 --> 00:21:05.840
<i>The light that is gone will shine no more</i>
<i>Alas! It shines no more</i>

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:07.510
Finis! You--

00:21:08.220 --> 00:21:10.010
What are you trying to do?!

00:21:14.060 --> 00:21:16.520
Everything should just disappear.

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:21.360
<i>If everything is an illusion</i>

00:21:21.690 --> 00:21:24.490
<i>Then everything shall disappear</i>

00:21:24.900 --> 00:21:27.740
<i>The true state of the world</i>

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:30.740
<i>Returning to nothingness</i>

00:21:31.410 --> 00:21:34.500
<i>If everything is destiny</i>

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:37.580
<i>Then everything</i>

00:21:38.250 --> 00:21:40.750
<i>Shall disappear</i>

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:43.920
<i>Life was created</i>

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:47.970
<i>To be guided</i>

00:21:48.340 --> 00:21:54.230
<i>To a world that ceases to exist</i>

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:16.460
<i>The darkness that beckons death</i>

00:22:18.290 --> 00:22:23.130
<i>The darkness that swallows madness</i>

00:22:24.760 --> 00:22:29.550
<i>People with frail hearts</i>

00:22:31.470 --> 00:22:36.430
<i>Close the doors to hope themselves</i>

00:22:38.270 --> 00:22:41.020
<i>The light</i>

00:22:41.650 --> 00:22:44.610
<i>That is gone</i>

00:22:44.820 --> 00:22:47.530
<i>Will shine no more</i>

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:50.660
<i>Alas!</i>

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:53.620
<i>It shines no more</i>

00:22:54.910 --> 00:22:57.910
<i>If everything is facade</i>

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:00.960
<i>And after everything has been abolished</i>

00:23:01.540 --> 00:23:04.550
<i>The true state of the world</i>

00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:07.630
<i>Returning to nothingness</i>

00:23:08.340 --> 00:23:11.220
<i>If everything is destiny</i>

00:23:11.640 --> 00:23:14.510
<i>And after everything has been abolished</i>

00:23:15.060 --> 00:23:17.850
<i>Life is yet again</i>

00:23:18.430 --> 00:23:20.890
<i>Created</i>

00:23:21.690 --> 00:23:25.020
<i>And guided</i>

00:23:25.110 --> 00:23:30.570
<i>To an unknown pulsating world</i>

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:37.240
What's that?

00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:39.160
A Symphony Killer!

00:23:39.750 --> 00:23:41.210
Hey. Over there!

00:23:45.790 --> 00:23:46.750
Could it be?

00:23:47.630 --> 00:23:49.130
Is that Finis?
